# Authentication Freeze

Authentication is **production-verified and frozen**. Policy: `docs/AUTH_FREEZE.md`.

## Do not modify (runtime)

- `apps/web/src/stores/authStore.ts`
- `apps/web/src/components/providers/AuthProvider.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/components/providers/AuthErrorBoundary.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/hooks/useAuth.ts`
- `apps/web/src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx`
- `apps/web/src/middleware.ts`
- `apps/web/src/lib/auth/session.ts`
- `apps/web/src/lib/auth/bootstrapDebug.ts`
- `apps/web/src/lib/cookies.ts`
- `apps/web/src/services/auth.ts`
- `apps/web/src/app/login/page.tsx`
- Auth wiring in `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx`

## Product work (e.g. Reception)

Use existing `useAuth` / `AppShell` as-is. Do **not** change bootstrap, restore, cookies, persist, or route-guard semantics.

## Allowed without freeze break

- Freeze docs (`docs/AUTH_FREEZE.md`)
- CI guard (`.github/workflows/web-auth-ci.yml`, `verify_auth_freeze.mjs`, auth regression tests only)

Any intentional auth change needs dedicated regression approval and must pass `test:auth-freeze` + `verify:auth-freeze`.
